            <ArticleTitle>Prominent pulmonary venous flow mimicking mitral regurgitation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1917-1918</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/echo.13755</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The present case highlights a potential pitfall in assessing mitral regurgitation severity due to the presence of similar colored prominent pulmonary vein signals in the left atrium during color Doppler examination.</AbstractText>
